			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2785650">
									

<p>Hmm&#8230; I think protagonist likability/relatability is one of my weakest points as a writer, but I tried to make Mitchell <em>kind</em> of likable and moral. He's skeptic, and even at the end of the line he won't admit to more than the faintest memories.</p>
<p>That being said, and appreciating your critique (hell, I'll take an upvote anyway I can get it), other than the D-Class headcannon of the tale, was there anything specific you didn't like about Mitch? Anything that turned you off? I'll admit he's a fairly bland character, but I thought he was empathetic. And if you didn't like him just 'cause he was so vanilla &#8212; well, that's cool, too. I just wanna know avenues to improve.</p>

							</div>

								
					
