														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2783756">
									

<p>Thanks are in order to Roget for their critique in the forum!</p>
<p>I agree there's too much exposition in the first half, but I'm not used to writing for an established&#8230; pretty much anything&#8230; nevermind something so in-depth with so much material and history as the SCP site. I was basically providing the exposition for my writing partner (who isn't familiar with SCP, and hasn't yet provided any feedback, the bastard), as well as trying to at least frame an internal logic within the story as to how the site was operated in order to suspend disbelief, as my biggest concern was &#8212; as Cyantreause mentioned &#8212; that this would go against many people's headcannon.</p>
<p>The last section was full of exposition regarding confabulation and the illusion of truth before I rewrote it probably half a dozen times into its current state.</p>

							</div>

								
					
